# Phase 03 — Debt Management

## Context Links
- Plan: [plan.md](./plan.md)
- Depends on: [phase-02-debt-book-management.md](./phase-02-debt-book-management.md)

## Overview
- **Priority:** P1
- **Status:** completed
- **Description:** Creditor can add/delete debts within a book. Debtor sees debts read-only. Scoped entirely to a specific `bookId`.

## Key Insights
- Debts are now scoped to `book_id`, not a global `owner_id`. All queries and actions receive `bookId`.
- Balance = `sum(debts.amount)` − `sum(payments.amount WHERE status='approved')`.
- Only `approved` payments count — `pending` payments shown separately (Phase 4).
- Existing `app/owner/` debt components can be adapted (not reused as-is — different imports, book-scoped).

## Architecture

```
app/books/[bookId]/
├── debts/
│   ├── page.tsx             # Full debts list (both roles see; only creditor can add/delete)
│   ├── new/page.tsx         # Add debt form (creditor only — guard in layout is enough)
│   └── actions.ts           # createDebt(bookId), deleteDebt(id)
lib/queries/
└── book-ledger.ts           # getLedgerTotals(bookId), getDebts(bookId), getPayments(bookId)
```

## Related Code Files
**Create:**
- `app/books/[bookId]/debts/page.tsx`
- `app/books/[bookId]/debts/new/page.tsx`
- `app/books/[bookId]/debts/actions.ts`
