- [x] Payments page (creditor view: pending queue + history)
- [x] Payments page (debtor view: own history with status)
- [x] Update `book-ledger.ts` with `getPendingPayments`, `getAllPayments`
- [x] Update webhook route for new field names
- [x] Test full flow: submit → pending → approve → balance updates

## Success Criteria
- Debtor submits → status shows "Chờ duyệt" for both users.
- Creditor approves → balance updates, status shows "Đã duyệt".
- Creditor rejects with reason → debtor sees "Bị từ chối" + reason, balance unchanged.
- Only approved payments affect balance total.

## Risk Assessment
- **Concurrent approvals**: at family scale, race condition is negligible. No optimistic locking needed.
- **Receipt URL in approval card**: use server-rendered signed URL (1h) — creditor views it on the same page load.
- **Rejection email fails**: log error, don't roll back the rejection. User can check dashboard.
- **Debtor resubmit after rejection**: allowed — they simply submit a new payment. Old rejected record stays in history.

## Security Considerations
- `approvePayment` / `rejectPayment` re-verify `me.id === book.creditor_id` server-side.
- RLS also enforces UPDATE on payments only by creditor of the book.
- `rejection_reason` is escaped before embedding in email HTML.
- `bookId` from route params, never from form body.
