- **Description:** Mobile-first polish across all new screens: book list, book dashboard, approval queue, payment history. Loading skeletons, empty states, status badges, Vietnamese copy, touch targets.

## Key Insights
- Bottom nav is now book-scoped (`/books/[bookId]/...`) and role-adaptive (creditor vs debtor links).
- Book list page is the new "home" — needs good empty state for fresh users.
- Approval card is the most interactive new element — needs clear affordance (confirm before approve, textarea for reject reason).
- Status badges must be immediately scannable on small screens.

## Architecture

```
components/
├── shell/
│   ├── app-header.tsx          # Remove role badge; show user email
│   └── bottom-nav.tsx          # Accept bookId + isCreditor instead of global role
├── states/
│   ├── empty-state.tsx         # Reuse existing
│   └── skeleton-card.tsx       # Reuse existing
app/books/
├── loading.tsx                 # Book list skeleton
├── [bookId]/
│   ├── loading.tsx             # Book dashboard skeleton
│   ├── error.tsx               # Error boundary
│   └── components/
│       ├── book-summary-card.tsx        # Totals + pending count
│       ├── payment-approval-card.tsx    # Approve/reject inline (Client Component)
│       ├── payment-status-badge.tsx     # Reusable badge chip
│       └── book-member-chip.tsx         # Shows partner name/role in header
```

## Implementation Steps

1. **`app-header.tsx`** — remove role badge; optionally show partner info via `book-member-chip` when inside a book route.

2. **`bottom-nav.tsx`** — accept `bookId?: string` and `isCreditor?: boolean`:
   - Outside book: show just "Sổ nợ" → `/books`.
   - Inside book (creditor): Home `/books/[bookId]` | Khoản nợ `/books/[bookId]/debts` | Thanh toán `/books/[bookId]/payments`.
   - Inside book (debtor): Home `/books/[bookId]` | Trả nợ `/books/[bookId]/payments/new` | Lịch sử `/books/[bookId]/payments`.

3. **Book list page polish**:
