# SoNo — Multi-user Debt Books + Payment Approval

Replace hardcoded owner/sister model with: any user creates a debt book with any other user (by email), payments submitted by debtor require creditor approval before counting toward balance.

## Goals
- Any authenticated user can create a debt book and designate another registered user as the debtor.
- Creditor manages debts in a book; debtor views balance and submits payments with receipts.
- Each payment starts as `pending` → creditor approves/rejects → only approved payments count.
- Email to creditor on new payment submission; email to debtor on rejection.
- Mobile-first, works on same tech stack.

## Architecture Change Summary

| Before | After |
|--------|-------|
| `profiles.role IN ('owner','sister')` | No fixed role in profiles |
| 1 global debt pool | `debt_books` table (creditor + debtor pair) |
| All payments auto-counted | Payments: pending → approved/rejected |
| Fixed `/owner` & `/sister` routes | `/books` list + `/books/[bookId]` per-book |

## Phases

| # | Phase | File | Status | Est |
|---|-------|------|--------|-----|
| 1 | Schema Migration | [phase-01-schema-migration.md](./phase-01-schema-migration.md) | completed | 3h |
| 2 | Debt Book Management | [phase-02-debt-book-management.md](./phase-02-debt-book-management.md) | completed | 4h |
| 3 | Debt Management | [phase-03-debt-management.md](./phase-03-debt-management.md) | completed | 3h |
| 4 | Payment Approval Flow | [phase-04-payment-approval.md](./phase-04-payment-approval.md) | completed | 6h |
| 5 | Notifications | [phase-05-notifications.md](./phase-05-notifications.md) | completed | 2h |
| 6 | UI Polish | [phase-06-ui-polish.md](./phase-06-ui-polish.md) | completed | 4h |

## Key Dependencies
- Phase 1 blocks everything (schema foundation).
- Phase 2 blocks 3 & 4 (debt books must exist before debts/payments).
- Phase 5 depends on Phase 4 (approval triggers emails).
- Phase 6 iterates over 2/3/4 screens.

## Files to Delete (Post-Migration)
- `app/owner/` (entire directory → replaced by per-book routes)
- `app/sister/` (entire directory)
- `lib/queries/ledger.ts` (replaced by book-scoped queries)
- `lib/queries/payments.ts` (absorbed into book queries)
- `lib/auth/get-current-user.ts` (role field removed; simplify)
- `supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql` (superseded by new migration)

## Out of Scope (YAGNI)
Multi-book settle/merge, debt categories, group debts (>2 users), email invites for unregistered users, real-time updates, admin panel.

## Success
- Two fresh accounts each create/view a shared debt book.
- Debtor submits payment → shows pending; creditor approves → balance updates.
- Owner receives email within 30s of payment submission.
- Debtor receives email on rejection.
